# Owner of the paths where a mistake costs the most: permissions, sign-in,
# media encryption, the media server and the TURN relay, outbound requests,
# release and update verification (the release scripts, the desktop bundle
# signing and its trust files), backup and restore, CI, the rules agents read
# and this file; and the paths that held the heaviest defects of the 2026-11
# defect hunt (the SFU, automod's link rules and the client's link reader they
# must match, the audit log's visibility, the plain text of pushes and
# snippets, the write gates of messages, conversations, poll votes and Talks,
# the channel visibility, the enforcement that removes a member from a Talk).
#
# This file has no effect by itself. GitHub requests a review from the owner,
# but a pull request only waits for it once main's ruleset has "Require review
# from Code Owners" turned on, which is a repository setting.

